WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.600
Matthew, Chapter Fifteen.

2
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:10.267
Then came to Jesus scribes and Pharisees, which were of Jerusalem, saying, Why do thy disciples transgress the tradition of the elders?

3
00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:13.067
for they wash not their hands when they eat bread.

4
00:00:13.067 --> 00:00:19.733
But he answered and said unto them, Why do ye also transgress the commandment of God by your tradition?

5
00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:28.800
For God commanded, saying, Honour thy father and mother: and, He that curseth father or mother, let him die the death.

6
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:39.867
But ye say, Whosoever shall say to his father or his mother, It is a gift, by whatsoever thou mightest be profited by me; And honour not his father or his mother, he shall be free.

7
00:00:39.867 --> 00:00:44.667
Thus have ye made the commandment of God of none effect by your tradition.

8
00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:55.867
Ye hypocrites, well did Esaias prophesy of you, saying, This people draweth nigh unto me with their mouth, and honoureth me with their lips; but their heart is far from me.

9
00:00:55.867 --> 00:01:01.200
But in vain they do worship me, teaching for doctrines the commandments of men.

10
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:12.000
And he called the multitude, and said unto them, Hear, and understand: Not that which goeth into the mouth defileth a man; but that which cometh out of the mouth, this defileth a man.

11
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:19.467
Then came his disciples, and said unto him, Knowest thou that the Pharisees were offended, after they heard this saying?

12
00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:25.467
But he answered and said, Every plant, which my heavenly Father hath not planted, shall be rooted up.

13
00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:29.067
Let them alone: they be blind leaders of the blind.

14
00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:33.067
And if the blind lead the blind, both shall fall into the ditch.

15
00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:36.933
Then answered Peter and said unto him, Declare unto us this parable.

16
00:01:36.933 --> 00:01:40.800
And Jesus said, Are ye also yet without understanding?

17
00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:48.800
Do not ye yet understand, that whatsoever entereth in at the mouth goeth into the belly, and is cast out into the draught?

18
00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:54.267
But those things which proceed out of the mouth come forth from the heart; and they defile the man.

19
00:01:54.267 --> 00:02:07.200
For out of the heart proceed evil thoughts, murders, adulteries, fornications, thefts, false witness, blasphemies: These are the things which defile a man: but to eat with unwashen hands defileth not a man.

20
00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:12.000
Then Jesus went thence, and departed into the coasts of Tyre and Sidon.

21
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:21.733
And, behold, a woman of Canaan came out of the same coasts, and cried unto him, saying, Have mercy on me, O Lord, thou Son of David; my daughter is grievously vexed with a devil.

22
00:02:21.733 --> 00:02:24.133
But he answered her not a word.

23
00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:29.733
And his disciples came and besought him, saying, Send her away; for she crieth after us.

24
00:02:29.733 --> 00:02:34.800
But he answered and said, I am not sent but unto the lost sheep of the house of Israel.

25
00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:39.067
Then came she and worshipped him, saying, Lord, help me.

26
00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:44.667
But he answered and said, It is not meet to take the children's bread, and to cast it to dogs.

27
00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:49.867
And she said, Truth, Lord: yet the dogs eat of the crumbs which fall from their masters' table.

28
00:02:49.867 --> 00:02:56.533
Then Jesus answered and said unto her, O woman, great is thy faith: be it unto thee even as thou wilt.

29
00:02:56.533 --> 00:02:59.733
And her daughter was made whole from that very hour.

30
00:02:59.733 --> 00:03:07.600
And Jesus departed from thence, and came nigh unto the sea of Galilee; and went up into a mountain, and sat down there.

31
00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:26.000
And great multitudes came unto him, having with them those that were lame, blind, dumb, maimed, and many others, and cast them down at Jesus' feet; and he healed them: Insomuch that the multitude wondered, when they saw the dumb to speak, the maimed to be whole, the lame to walk,

32
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.000
and the blind to see: and they glorified the God of Israel.

33
00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:42.400
Then Jesus called his disciples unto him, and said, I have compassion on the multitude, because they continue with me now three days, and have nothing to eat: and I will not send them away fasting, lest they faint in the way.

34
00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:51.733
And his disciples say unto him, Whence should we have so much bread in the wilderness, as to fill so great a multitude?

35
00:03:51.733 --> 00:03:55.200
And Jesus saith unto them, How many loaves have ye?

36
00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:58.133
And they said, Seven, and a few little fishes.

37
00:03:58.133 --> 00:04:01.200
And he commanded the multitude to sit down on the ground.

38
00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:10.267
And he took the seven loaves and the fishes, and gave thanks, and brake them, and gave to his disciples, and the disciples to the multitude.

39
00:04:10.267 --> 00:04:16.133
And they did all eat, and were filled: and they took up of the broken meat that was left seven baskets full.

40
00:04:16.133 --> 00:04:20.933
And they that did eat were four thousand men, beside women and children.

41
00:04:20.933 --> 00:04:25.867
And he sent away the multitude, and took ship, and came into the coasts of Magdala.

